      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-143236",
      ":question/problem": "A political science researcher estimates that approximately $75%$ of all students at a large university are registered voters. Find a lower bound for sample size $n$ needed to ensure that the margin of error of the $99%$ confidence interval for the proportion of the population of students who are registered voters is at most $0.06$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(Z > 2.576) = 0.005$, where $Z\u223cN(0, 1)$.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
